{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:58:12.359474Z","id":"9b9f8d251fddf878ac68e1943e22942251149f6f835962cbce5de66b441f9331","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/caps/home.ts passes {x, y, w, h} from the page unchanged and HomeHost._rect builds a Rect from it. The frame's offset in the shell and the WebView's place on screen are not applied, so an anchored menu would be misplaced wherever the frame does not start at the screen's top left. Launcher's own HomeActions ignores the anchor (a bottom sheet). Whoever implements HomeActions.menu for the home route (plan Task 3) must map it, as host_protocol.dart's attestation maps pointer positions.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":352},"end":{"line":369},"content_hash":"89575e5821e693c40b8b51b085c7a14e64a879dc2d6913be55f1d7028971cf0a"},"summary":"home.menu's rect is taken as Flutter logical pixels as given: CSS pixels in the page's frame, not mapped to the screen","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:58:12.359574Z","id":"a891774fd391ab5ce1b972804caeea6a888e0b7e41bff75143a11b8a5201c67b","body":{"detail":"No daemon route serves AppIcons' cached icons under the home app's origin; a data URL needs none and no cross-app read grant. It relies on the artifact CSP leaving img-src open (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs sets none) and grows apps() answers and every apps event by each icon's size.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":389},"end":{"line":405},"content_hash":"beafba81f576197bfca659cc09143bde8c4ef47c501c4efff9fdace12c434036"},"summary":"apps() gives an app's own icon as a data:image/svg+xml URL of the cleaned SVG, not a daemon-served URL as spec 2026-10-16 section 2 says","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_install.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:25:17.928487Z","id":"a47614ec7aae77343e9af4f3d78cdce1e641cd2a7a5a64bfec9c0094d8af5c13","body":{"detail":"ensureHomeApp installs through Installer.install, which writes the lineage entry with role installed and fromBundle: !mine (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart:195-204); the home bundle is signed by its release key, never this install's, so mine is false. lib/app.dart passes fromBundleOf(_lineages) to the agent loop. Whether the home app, which the person changes by commenting, should be treated as code from a bundle is for plan Tasks 6 and 7 to settle.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"6d33ffada4a2495fed685ccbeec3b3dd77b78805eb8be9abcb38e149cd7999ee"},"summary":"The installed home app is recorded fromBundle: true, so the agent changes it under the bundle isolation rules (fromBundleOf), as any app installed from a file","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:25:17.928714Z","id":"ca483c0424926775377acaa90cde0b81a9817b30496ce19177cf408cc66fed73","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:35246b56","summary":"Fixed in 35246b56: AppScreen._onScreen (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart) moves home.menu's rect by the page view's place in the window (the surface widget's localToGlobal) before HomeHost.call builds the Rect. In app mode the shell's content frame starts at the WebView's top left (macOS integration run: the home app's grid drawn from the WebView's 0,0). flutter test test/home/home_route_test.dart: 'a menu rect from the page is moved onto the screen' passes (rect {x:5,y:100} on a view at (10,40) reaches HomeActions.menu as Rect.fromLTWH(15, 140, 60, 70)); +7 All tests passed.","supersedes":"9b9f8d251fddf878ac68e1943e22942251149f6f835962cbce5de66b441f9331","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_install.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:33:46.084271Z","id":"4d47246a3f92bf1608f37b8eb15377ce7e749ae87655731cd818f409439ec90a","body":{"detail":"If HomeSettings.save throws, _installHome (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart:894-898) returns without settingsChanged, yet host.settings.homeAppId now holds the new ID, so the next HomeRoute rebuild for any other reason switches to the home app while home.json does not record it (the next launch adopts it by lineage).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"bc5003c9d1387fdbb68ae8e26d283a5e0c883370b52cc32099cc3ff97b0e4d56"},"suggested_fix":"Save a copy first, or restore the previous ID on failure.","summary":"ensureHomeApp sets settings.homeAppId before save; a failed save leaves the ID in memory, contrary to its doc 'with settings unchanged'","tags":["review","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:35:57.495649Z","id":"419b2696baf76ee0790f72ce4868a410d4eb193dbec32ef24bca9acaa8c00606","body":{"detail":"UpdateSheet in its modified form has only Keep mine and Update, but showBundleSheet is dismissible, so a null answer is possible. Asking again on the next start is the chosen reading of 'asks once per release' in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-home-screen-app-design.md section 5; treating a dismissal as Keep mine is the other.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"478e66199588ae9c9a8d0cfff3eb963ba9143f7fa3eabbc0d45b79a801452ab6"},"summary":"Closing the update sheet without answering (back, or the barrier) returns HomeUpdateResult.none and the same release asks again at the next start; only Keep mine stops the asking","tags":["home-app","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:47:28.557047Z","id":"25d12051d1e7edb4a0c56e63ca59c49f35a4a8311d8ddbd3ddf2d185d63b37f5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"419b2696baf76ee0790f72ce4868a410d4eb193dbec32ef24bca9acaa8c00606","summary":"Owner's decision (2026-10-16): closing the update sheet without answering asks again at the next start; keep the current behaviour.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_install.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:05:33.759726Z","id":"8eb8209949495e4d4c098b3dc115fba9a428c289abd6e155834a0749d75d9538","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:df081df6","summary":"Fixed in df081df6: ensureHomeApp restores the previous homeAppId when save throws. Evidence: flutter test test/home/home_install_test.dart 'a home.json that cannot be written leaves the settings in memory unchanged' passes.","supersedes":"4d47246a3f92bf1608f37b8eb15377ce7e749ae87655731cd818f409439ec90a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_route.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:05:54.624167Z","id":"2be1402a9b0f7fcf0b83be6c7e6b596cb9fec8e4e45adb64b2e15f655cd7f452","body":{"detail":"HomeRoute lifts its cover and stops the 10 s rule only on HomeHost.shown (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart, case 'shown'), which apps/clax_app/home/home.js calls from an effect once its grid, empty state or load error is drawn. A version the agent writes without that call shows the fallback banner every launch although it works. The agent's prompt (apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/) and the kit's fake host (apps/clax_app/assets/kit/fake-home.js, which has no shown member) and its tool text (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/kit_tool.dart:194) do not mention shown() yet; they should, and the kit's tests could fail a home page that never calls it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"7973fccd63e299579be0c966fa32d22831288f80b6a48393c516be78034af601"},"summary":"A home app version that never calls home.shown() falls back to the built-in home screen 10 s after every load","tags":["home","follow-up","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_route.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:05:54.624351Z","id":"81d5a0ac9bda02b1e28dd9c4dd2e302f9247f0d9c33d2fd7a3ee9a81694b3b4c","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the shell posts Ready at the content frame's load event, which can come after the page's first home round trips and its shown(), so a fine page could be timed out and covered by the banner. The rule counts from the route loading the page (first mount, and each reload after Undo or Reset); a later broken version that loads is caught only by 'This app stopped loading'. Would need the shell to tag shown() with the document it came from.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"7973fccd63e299579be0c966fa32d22831288f80b6a48393c516be78034af601"},"summary":"Restarting the 10 s rule at each frame-load ready, so a new version that loads but never draws falls back too","tags":["home","revisit:after the device check of the home app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_route.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:10:36.765743Z","id":"87692548cf543d0f4e2e48699c74cd48fed76ebd53c40064157d40dc2c640893","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:09d999ca","summary":"The prompts (system.md, single-call.md) tell the agent to call home.shown() once the grid is drawn and never drop it; fake-home.js counts calls in home.shownCount; kit_tool.dart's fake-home.js API text names shown() and how to test it; home/tests/home.test.js 'the shipped page calls shown() exactly once over the kit's fake host'. npx playwright test e2e/home-app.spec.ts: 8 passed (the inspect-view run reports 21 passed); flutter test of home_bundle, home_install, home_update, kit_tool and prompt tests: +54 all passed; scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check exits 0.","supersedes":"2be1402a9b0f7fcf0b83be6c7e6b596cb9fec8e4e45adb64b2e15f655cd7f452","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
